Subject: text-shimmer-v2: no global font-smoothing rule, and the swept copy exists only while sweeping

What: the sheet drops its `* { -webkit-font-smoothing; -moz-osx-font-smoothing;
text-rendering }` rule, and the swept copy of the text mounts only while the
shimmer runs (`run()`), so the sweep animation and its will-change apply to an
element that exists only then; the `data-run` attribute goes.
Why: the `*` rule restyled every element of any app that imports the sheet. The
swept copy is a second full copy of the text plus a gradient clipped to its glyphs,
and a transcript holds one shimmer per tool row: 39 of 40 were idle in a measured
lab session, each paying for the copy and the clipped gradient while doing nothing.
The original text-shimmer sheet in this kit carries the same fix.

diff --git a/src/v2/components/text-shimmer-v2.css b/src/v2/components/text-shimmer-v2.css
